# 2026-09-04land, +1 (49 -> 50), roster 5a50bc47 -> 0a9e8634: `drop_fn_for`'s
# per-candidate `c->trait_name == "Drop"` identity test. THE BARE NAME IS THE
# CARRIED DECISION, not an oversight: `collect_impl`'s `builtin_marker_` merges a
# `trait Drop` declared in ANY package into the destructor trait — 109 fixtures in
# this tree declare their own and none imports `logos.lang.drop` — so in this tree
# the destructor trait's IDENTITY *is* the bare name. The site next door,
# `explicit_destructor_call` (sema_expr.cpp), records the same decision in the same
# words. What the test replaces is worse than a bare name: keying the destructor on
# the MANGLED SYMBOL `<T>__drop`, which ran any inherent or other-trait `drop` at
# scope exit (PROBES.md 2026-09-04land, root 3).
# ── 2026-09-10d — THE BARE TYPE NAME `Vec`, BOTH DIRECTIONS ─────────────────
# FACT 4 moves in three files and FACT 5 in two, from ONE structural change: the
# stdlib container `logos.mem.collections.vec.Vec<T>` was decided by its BARE
# NAME at nineteen sites, and now is not.
#
# CONSUMERS, -11 comparisons (sema_expr.cpp -8 by this class + the two-line
# lambda form collapsing to one line, sema_stmt.cpp -1, sema.cpp -1), all
# replaced by the free `is_stdlib_vec` in sema_impl.hpp (+1 there): the
# is_stdlib_box idiom, bare name PLUS `pkg.empty() || pkg ==
# "logos.mem.collections.vec"`. sema_expr.cpp 8407 (the A16/A17 `Vec::get`
# move-out refusal), 19028/19035/19049 (quote_item! cursors), 20067/20078
# (quote_expr! cursors), 21727 (the `vec!` element hint), 22097 and 25166 (the
# `#[fn_macro]` / item-macro signatures); sema_stmt.cpp 7614 (`for x in &v` ->
# `as_slice`); sema.cpp 2322 (`&Vec<T>` -> `&[T]`).
#
# PRODUCERS, FACT 5: make_generic_struct 8 -> 1, make_synth_generic_struct
# 8 -> 15. All seven `make_generic_struct("Vec", …)` mints became
# `make_synth_generic_struct`, and `Vec` joined `synth_owner_pkg_`'s table —
# #102's own fix applied to the one type it had missed. Before it, the mint went
# through `resolve_struct_pkg_`, whose first tier is `sema_key(cur_package_,
# name)`, so a module declaring its own `Vec` had the COMPILER'S synthesised
# type handed the USER'S package.
#
# MEASURED on the unmodified compiler, three shapes: a package-local
# `struct Vec<T> { a: i64, b: i64 }` passed as `&[i64]` compiled clean and
# SEGV'd (rc 139, 7 read as the data pointer and 3 as the length); a package's
# own `Vec` with its own `get` returning i64 was REFUSED with the stdlib
# sentence, prescribing `.borrow`/`.remove`/`.pop`, which that type lacks; and a
# list comprehension in such a module emitted `'func.call' op
# 'Vec$G1$i64__push' does not reference a valid function`, an internal MLIR
# verification failure with no user diagnostic. Soundness-queue rows
# `localvec_ref_coerces_to_slice_admits` and `localvec_get_refused_by_stdlib_rule`
# closed; pinned in PAIRS one token apart (pass/vec_pkg_slice_coerce_stdlib +
# fail/vec_pkg_slice_coerce_local, pass/vec_pkg_get_local_own_method +
# fail/vec_pkg_get_stdlib_noncopy, pass/vec_pkg_listcomp_local_homonym +
# fail/vec_pkg_listcomp_annot_local, and pass/vec_pkg_for_ref_stdlib).
#
# ⚠ WHAT THIS DOES NOT CLOSE, AND IT IS A TWELFTH MEMBER THIS CENSUS CANNOT SEE:
# `for x in &v` over a package-local `Vec` now falls through to the IntoIterator
# desugar, which resolves `find_func_candidates(base + "__into_iter")` on the
# BARE struct name and finds the stdlib's `ref_Vec__into_iter`. The name is
# CONCATENATED into a method symbol, so it is neither a comparison (FACT 4) nor
# a literal argument (FACT 5). Soundness-queue row
# `localvec_for_ref_names_stdlib_as_slice` stays open and was RE-POINTED at it.
# PROBES.md 2026-09-10d.
