# sema_expr.cpp 162 -> 160, 2026-09-10h. The Deref/DerefMut bound-autoderef
# fallback (`lower_method_call`) is the LAST lang-item trait decision in this
# file that was keyed on a bare spelling, and it was one decision policed
# asymmetrically: the `== "DerefMut"` arm was always visible to FACT 4, the
# `!= "Deref"` arm was not until 2026-09-10g widened the matcher. Both literals
# are gone, replaced by `bound_is_deref_lang_item`, which resolves the bound's
# canonical registry key through `trait_key_is_lang_item` against
# kDerefLangPkg = "logos.lang.ops" — the same instrument `bound_is_copy_lang_item`
# uses for kCopyLangPkg. MEASURED on the unmodified compiler before the change:
# a package-local `trait Deref<T> { fn deref(&self) -> &T; }` gave a type
# parameter operator-deref power, so `t.get()` — provided by NO bound —
# compiled, linked and RAN, printing got42 with exit 0; a local `Deref` with no
# `deref` method at all reached mlir-gen and died there ("'func.call' op
# 'W__deref' does not reference a valid function"), an internal failure where a
# user diagnostic belongs. Both now refuse with the sentence
# `trait.method-dispatch.no-bound-provides-method` specifies. Pinned in PAIRS
# one token apart: pass/deref_bound_lang_item_autoderef (imports
# logos.lang.ops, RUNS, asserts got42) and
# fail/deref_bound_local_homonym_no_autoderef (declares its own homonym).
